      "message": "This is the code I was referring to in my previous comment above. How should instanced indirect draws be abstracted? The `DrawPassCommands::List::drawIndirect` and `DrawPassCommands::List::drawIndexedIndirect` functions inherently support instances (since the instance count/offset are encoded in the indirect buffer).\n\nI can imagine changing this to just check if `fIndirect` is assigned above and routing to one of these functions. Though in the case where an indirect draw uses a CPU-populated static vertex/index buffer, I think `fTemplateCount`/`realVertexCount` above will need to be communicated to the compute shader somehow so it can write it into the indirect buffer (unless we map the buffer indirect buffer first and write the vertex/index counts on the CPU).",
